  "slug": "genetic-effects-1a8b",
  "summary": "New preprints extend GWAS fine-mapping beyond expression to splicing, structural variants, allele-specific chromatin and MPRA/CRISPR validation in relevant cells.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is mapping disease-associated noncoding variants to effector genes in disease-relevant tissues and cell types. Several studies move beyond gene abundance. In 1,149 IBD colon samples, joint eQTL and sQTL mapping implicates NMD and immune pathways. Colocalization of 338 type 2 diabetes signals with adipose expression, splicing and transcript usage finds RNA features that gene-level eQTLs miss. Pangenome genotyping in CARTaGENE adds 103 structural-variant eQTLs. Functional resolution is reaching single variants. MPRA and CRISPR perturbation in chondrocytes link osteoarthritis variant rs1895062 to PAPPA. In human microglia, allele-specific open chromatin indicates that the alcohol use disorder variant rs7307261 alters ETS-factor binding. CELL-X prioritizes beta cells and genes such as SLC30A8 and TCF7L2 from islet single-cell data. The IGVF Catalog provides infrastructure by integrating 657 datasets. Studies of desert selection, hominin-derived variation and adipose transposable elements are more peripheral.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
